INSTITUTE  (2SPNPCM,2GERFRK,2FR SAC,3POLLOU,2FR PAR,2ITYBAU,
            3CZRCHU,2UK MAN,3CROZAG,2ZZZCER,2SPNUPC,2PRTLIS,
            2SPNSEU,2GRCTUA,2GERMUN,2SPNSAU,2ITYPAD,2GRCARU,
            4ZZZDUB,3INDTRM,2SPNVAL,4RUSFEI,2AUSTHV,2SWTPSI,
            2ZZZGEL,2UK YRK,2GERKFK,2JPNTIT,1USAORL,2AUSVIE,
            2ITYUBO,2ITYBOL,2ITYTRI,3RUMBUC,2SWTBAS,3AULCBR)
           (2SPNSPN) Universidad de Granada
REFERENCE  (J,PR/C,97,054616,2018)
           (J,EPJ/CS,146,11022,2017)
            Cross section at 0.2-1.4 eV and 100-10000 eV in figs
           (J,NDS,119,65,2014)
            Preliminary cross section at 140-165 eV in fig
EXP-YEAR   (2010)
REL-REF    (I,,C.Guerrero+,J,EPJ/A,49,27,2013)
            Description of facility, neutron production, moderator
           (M,,M.Barbagallo+,J,EPJ/A,49,156,2013)
            Description of flux determination procedure
           (I,,C.Guerrero+,J,NIM/A,608,424,2009)
            Description of the TAC detector
FACILITY   (SYNCY,2ZZZCER) CERN nTOF facility.
            Protons (7E+12 protons/pulse) were accelerated to
             20 GeV.
INC-SOURCE (SPALL) 1.2E+5 neutrons/pulse were produced in a
            cylindrical Pb spallation target (1.3 t in mass,
            40 cm in length, 60 cm in diameter).
           Neutrons were moderated by Pb target itself, 1 cm
            layer of demineralized water and 4 cm layer of
            borated water (H2O + 1.28% H3BO3 mass fraction).
           The neutron beam at sample position can be
            approximated by Gaussian shape with sigma=0.62 cm.
           Flux was measured at the same time by SiMoN [6Li(n,t)
            reaction] and MGAS [10B(n,a) and 235U(n,f) reactions]
            detectors.
           Flux was also measured by PTB and PPAC [235U(n,f)
            reaction] detectors in the same year, but not at the
            same time.
SAMPLE     36.5-mg 241AmO2 infiltrated into a 305-mg Al2O3
            matrix. The 241Am mass (32.23+/-0.19 mg) was
            determined by calorimetry at JRC Karlsruhe.
           237Np (~0.9 mg) and 240Pu (~0.016 mg) were detected
            as impurities during resonance analysis.
DETECTOR   (BAF2) Total Absorption Calorimeter (TAC) made of 40
            BaF2 crystals (15 cm in length covering ~95% of the
            solid angle) to detect in coincidence (nearly) all
            the gamma rays coming from capture reactions.
           (SI) Silicon flux monitor (SiMon) consisted of thin
            6Li deposit on thin Mylar foil surrounded by a set of
            four silicon detectors outside the neutron beam for
            recording the tritons and alpha particles from the
            6Li(n,a)3H reaction.
METHOD     Total energy absorption.
           (TOF) Flight path length of 185.59+/-0.02 m.
MONITOR    (79-AU-197(N,G)79-AU-198,,SIG)
            Absolute normalization to the saturated 4.9 eV
            capture resonance of 197Au.
CORRECTION Background was subtracted by performing the following
            additional runs:
            - dummy sample (Al canning + Al2O3 matrix)
            - Al canning
            - no sample
            - graphite sample (to determine TAC response to
              sample scattered neutrons)
            - 241Am without beam
            - no sample without beam
STATUS     (APRVD) Approved by Emilio Mendoza (2018-06-06)
HISTORY    (20180604C) On+ED
           (20260115A) On. Resolution function moved to 009.
ENDBIB             100
NOCOMMON             0          0
ENDSUBENT          103
SUBENT        23369002   20180604   20180903   20180809       2266
BIB                  5         13
REACTION   (95-AM-241(N,G)95-AM-242,,RYL)
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-S) Uncertainty due to counting statistics
           (ERR-1) Systematic due to systematic effect excluding:
           (ERR-2) - uncertainty due to neutron fluence shape
                                (1% at En < 100 eV, otherwise 2%)
           (ERR-3) - uncertainty due to normalization      (2.7%)
CORRECTION The background has been subtracted, including the
            resonant background due to fission in 241Am.
           The only background components which have not been
            subtracted are the ones due to capture reactions in
            the 240Pu and 237Np impurities.
STATUS     (TABLE) Data received from E.Mendoza via E.Dupont
